From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: PS5: A title process's memory is copied through a pipe that never blocks.

A helper's ReadProcessMemory or WriteProcessMemory of a process in the title is served by the server thread, which copies
the memory through a pipe it both writes and reads (so an unmapped address makes the kernel answer EFAULT instead of the
server faulting). The pipe was blocking and a chunk was 16 KiB. A blocking write the pipe cannot take at once waits for a
reader. On FreeBSD, which the console's kernel comes from, a blocking pipe write of 8 KiB or more is a direct write that
waits for the reader to take it (not checked on the console's kernel itself), and any pipe with less room than the chunk
does the same. The only reader is the waiting thread itself, so the server stopped
for good.

A tester's Risk of Rain 2 in the title froze at loading three sessions out of three (tester-freeze-loading-2026-11-01). Each
time its Steam crash handler had started steamerrorreporter64.exe -pid=<game> in a helper, and within seconds Wine's tick
count, which only the server's main loop advances, stopped (976.659 for ten minutes in session 2). Every later server
call waited, and so did the title's 30 s registry save, 3000 ms each time. Before Alpha 7 almost nothing in a helper read
a title process's memory; a minidump of a game in the title does it at its first stack.

Both ends are now non-blocking, a short write copies what it took and goes on, and a short read into a target that is not
writable drains what is left, as before. The copy lives in wine/ps5/pw_wine_copy_pipe.h, copied here by
tools/build-wine-ps5.sh. Host test tests/test_pw_wine_copy_pipe.c covers whole copies of 1 B to 256 KiB both ways, a copy
that stops at a no-access page, and a pipe shrunk to 4 KiB. With the old blocking pipe that last case hangs on Linux, and
the test's alarm ends it. Console case dump-server64-title (tests/suspend-server-probe.c --mode=read). Not run on a console.
---
diff --git a/server/ptrace.c b/server/ptrace.c
index 3852c54..43c43d1 100644
--- a/server/ptrace.c
+++ b/server/ptrace.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include <sys/wait.h>
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
+#include "pw_wine_copy_pipe.h"
 #endif
 #ifdef HAVE_SYS_PTRACE_H
 # include <sys/ptrace.h>
@@ -481,54 +482,12 @@ static int read_process_memory_ptrace( struct thread *thread, client_ptr_t ptr,
  * not mapped makes the kernel answer EFAULT instead of the server taking the fault. */
 static int ps5_copy_pipe[2] = { -1, -1 };
 
-static int ps5_copy_pipe_open(void)
-{
-    if (ps5_copy_pipe[0] == -1 && pipe( ps5_copy_pipe ))
-    {
-        ps5_copy_pipe[0] = ps5_copy_pipe[1] = -1;
-        return 0;
-    }
-    return 1;
-}
-
-/* from this process's memory into dest (read), or from src into this process's memory (write) */
+/* Through a non-blocking pipe (patch 2453, wine/ps5/pw_wine_copy_pipe.h): this thread is its only writer and its only
+ * reader, and a blocking write it could not finish waited for itself. A crash reporter in a helper dumping a game in the
+ * title stopped the server for good. */
 static data_size_t ps5_copy_memory( int writing, char *local, const char *target, data_size_t size )
 {
-    data_size_t done = 0;
-    char scratch[4096];
-
-    if (!ps5_copy_pipe_open()) return 0;
-    while (done < size)
-    {
-        data_size_t chunk = size - done < 16384 ? size - done : 16384;
-        ssize_t count;
-
-        if (writing)
-        {
-            if (write( ps5_copy_pipe[1], local + done, chunk ) != (ssize_t)chunk) break;
-            count = read( ps5_copy_pipe[0], (char *)target + done, chunk );
-            if (count < (ssize_t)chunk)
-            {
-                /* the target was not writable all the way: what is left in the pipe is not wanted */
-                for (;;)
-                {
-                    long left = 0;
-                    if (ioctl( ps5_copy_pipe[0], FIONREAD, &left ) || left <= 0) break;
-                    if (read( ps5_copy_pipe[0], scratch, left < (long)sizeof(scratch) ? left : (long)sizeof(scratch) ) <= 0) break;
-                }
-                if (count > 0) done += count;
-                break;
-            }
-        }
-        else
-        {
-            count = write( ps5_copy_pipe[1], target + done, chunk );
-            if (count <= 0) break;
-            if (read( ps5_copy_pipe[0], local + done, count ) != count) break;
-        }
-        done += count;
-    }
-    return done;
+    return pw_wine_copy_memory( ps5_copy_pipe, writing, local, target, size );
 }
 
 /* Another process's memory: a helper process runs each Windows program but the title's own, and its memory is
